+// vectorised direct sweep and a NEON quantized dot; not ARMv7 either, which has NEON (see the guard
+// in llamafile/sgemm.cpp).
+//
+// `ggml_conv_1d_direct_ok` refuses a convolution whose weights exceed the cache budget or whose
+// activation is short relative to its channel count -- and on a VITS vocoder that is the LARGEST
+// bucket, 41 calls of IC*K=960, OC=384 at OL=275, 36% of a synthesis. Those fall to the batched
+// im2col below, which runs against the DEQUANTIZED kernel because the block at the top of
+// `ggml_compute_forward_conv_2d_impl` has already expanded it. On a core with no vector unit that is
+// the worst of both: F32 arithmetic over 1.47 MB of weights where the stored form is 207 KB.
+//
+// Measured on a Pi Zero W at that shape, all arms verified identical:
+//     F32 GEMM (what this replaces)                29.7 MMAC/s
+//     q4_0 x q8_0 through this path               167.9 MMAC/s   5.65x
+//
+// The folded kernel layout [IC*KH*KW, OC] that loom's ggml-0013 introduced so the weights could be
+// block-quantized at all IS a GEMM's weight matrix, so nothing is repacked here: the stored kernel is
+// handed to the GEMM as it sits, and only the im2col patches are quantized.
+//
